[16.259723, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[16.326769, "o", "[HIGH  ] M15-01 (15.1) the inference image reached end of patch on 2026-09-15 (dlc: 365 days after release): it gets no more securi\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-03 (15.2) the model container runs without network isolation: code in it can call out to the internet and use the exec\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-05 (15.2) Studio notebooks can reach the internet (PublicInternetOnly (the default): direct internet access through a \r\n[HIGH  ] M15-08 (15.2) execution role tsg-summariser-exec has AmazonSageMakerFullAccess (AWS: 'fairly broad'); s3:* on *: everythin\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-10 (15.2) ds-alice may pass tsg-summariser-exec to SageMaker AI: a job or notebook they start runs with the production\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-10 (15.2) ds-bob may pass tsg-summariser-exec to SageMaker AI: a job or notebook they start runs with the production r\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-11 (15.2) ds-alice may create a presigned Studio URL for bob: they sign in as that profile, with its files and executi\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-11 (15.2) ds-bob may create a presigned Studio URL for alice: they sign in as that profile, with its files and executi\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-12 (15.2) secret-looking value in the container Environment (HF_TOKEN): DescribeModel returns it to ds-alice, ds-bob\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-14 (15.3) tsg-helpdesk-app may call InvokeEndpoint from anywhere (no aws:SourceVpce condition): stolen keys work from \r\n[HIGH  ] M15-14 (15.3) ds-alice may call InvokeEndpoint from anywhere (no aws:SourceVpce condition): stolen keys work from the inte\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-14 (15.3) ds-bob may call InvokeEndpoint from anywhere (no aws:SourceVpce condition): stolen keys work from the intern\r\n"]
[16.326977, "o", "[HIGH  ] M15-15 (15.3) the sagemaker.runtime interface endpoint has the default policy (full access): credentials from any AWS acco\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-16 (15.3) EnableSSMAccess on a production variant: shell access into the inference container for ds-alice, ds-bob; AWS\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-17 (15.3) the endpoint's model points straight at an S3 path, not at an approved Model Registry version: nobody's appr\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-18 (15.3) ds-alice may call UpdateModelPackage: a data scientist can approve their own model version (no four-eyes)\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-18 (15.3) ds-bob may call UpdateModelPackage: a data scientist can approve their own model version (no four-eyes)\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-19 (15.3) the deployed model files are not safetensors-only: pytorch_model.bin (pickle: imports builtins.print)\r\n[HIGH  ] M15-20 (15.3) ds-alice, ds-bob may overwrite the files the endpoint loads (s3://amzn-s3-demo-tsg-models/tsg-summariser/v1/\r\n19 HIGH, 13 MEDIUM, 3 LOW  (35 findings)\r\n"]
