[30.183774, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[30.240089, "o", "[MEDIUM] M15-02 (15.1) the image is pinned by tag, not by digest: the same tag can point at different bytes over time\r\n[MEDIUM] M15-04 (15.2) the model has no VpcConfig: model downloads don't go through your VPC, so your S3 endpoint policy and flow l\r\n[MEDIUM] M15-06 (15.2) sg-0a1b2c3d4e5f60031 allows inbound from itself and is shared by alice, bob: AWS warns users in the VPC coul\r\n[MEDIUM] M15-07 (15.2) the Studio domain has no KmsKeyId: notebooks' EFS and EBS volumes use an AWS managed key, whose key policy y\r\n[MEDIUM] M15-09 (15.2) tsg-summariser-exec trust policy has no aws:SourceArn: any SageMaker AI resource, in any account, could be t\r\n[MEDIUM] M15-09 (15.2) tsg-ds-exec trust policy has no aws:SourceArn: any SageMaker AI resource, in any account, could be the one a\r\n[MEDIUM] M15-21 (15.3) no file hashes recorded for the deployed model: nobody can prove the files running are the ones approved\r\n[MEDIUM] M15-21 (15.3) licence not recorded: AWS says reviewing model licences is your job\r\n[MEDIUM] M15-22 (15.3) no approval gate: nothing checks formats, hashes, licence and approver before a version becomes Approved (ch\r\n[MEDIUM] M15-23 (15.2) no SCP requires network isolation and a VPC on CreateModel: an admin's quick test can still ship a container\r\n[MEDIUM] M15-24 (15.4) data capture (full prompts and answers) is written without a KmsKeyId of yours\r\n[MEDIUM] M15-24 (15.4) data capture goes to amzn-s3-demo-tsg-analytics, a bucket other teams read: captured prompts are as sensitiv\r\n[MEDIUM] M15-25 (15.4) no CloudTrail data events for AWS::SageMaker::Endpoint: InvokeEndpoint is a data event, and trails don't log\r\n[LOW   ] M15-13 (15.2) KmsKeyId on an endpoint with ml.g5.xlarge (NVMe instance storage): AWS says you can't use a KMS key on an in\r\n[LOW   ] M15-26 (15.4) no alarm on Invocation4XXErrors or invocation volume: probing and abuse show up there first\r\n[LOW   ] M15-27 (15.4) the monitoring plan relies on SageMaker Model Monitor or Clarify: both are no longer open to new customers\r\n\r\n"]
