[115.25075, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[115.252824, "o", "python3 evaluate.py hardened\r\n"]
[115.294554, "o", "  A1   blocked  Booby-trapped model file: the weights are a pickle, and loading it runs code in the container\r\n         . no pickle-based weights: nothing ran at load\r\n  A2   blocked  Artifact swap after approval: a data scientist overwrites the files the endpoint loads\r\n         . ds-bob writes into s3://amzn-s3-demo-tsg-models/tsg-summariser/v2/: DENIED (explicit Deny in the bucket policy of amzn-s3-demo-tsg-models)\r\n  A3   blocked  Unapproved model to production: a hotfix model straight from a notebook onto the live endpoint\r\n         . ds-bob CreateModel on model/tsg-summariser-hotfix: DENIED (no identity policy allows it (implicit deny))\r\n  A4   blocked  Self-approval: the author approves their own model version\r\n         . ds-bob registered version 3, then approves it himself: DENIED (explicit Deny in the identity policy)\r\n  A5   blocked  Data out of the container: code in the model container posts tickets to the internet\r\n"]
[115.294631, "o", "         . code in the container posts a ticket to https://collector.example.net: blocked (network isolation: no outbound calls, no AWS credentials in the container)\r\n  A6   blocked  Container credentials: code in the container reads another team's bucket with the execution role\r\n         . code in the container asks for the execution role's credentials: none (network isolation: no outbound calls, no AWS credentials in the container)\r\n  A7   blocked  Stolen app keys: InvokeEndpoint from the internet\r\n         . the app's leaked keys, used from a laptop on the internet: DENIED (no identity policy allows it (implicit deny))\r\n  A8   blocked  Outsider through the private endpoint: someone else's account sends data out via AnyCompany's VPC endpoint\r\n         . someone in the VPC uses their OWN account's keys, through AnyCompany's runtime endpoint, to send tickets to their endpoint: DENIED (the sagemaker.runtime VPC endpoint policy does not allow it)\r\n  A9   blocked  Shell into the endpoint: SSM access on the production container\r\n         . EnableSSMAccess is off on every variant: no shell to open\r\n  A10  blocked  Studio exfiltration: a notebook uploads data to the internet\r\n         . a notebook uploads a ticket export to https://collector.example.net: blocked (VpcOnly: no route to the internet)\r\n  A11  blocked  Studio impersonation: a presigned URL for someone else's profile\r\n         . ds-bob creates a presigned Studio URL for alice's profile: DENIED (no identity policy allows it (implicit deny))\r\n  A12  blocked  PassRole escalation: a job started by a data scientist runs as the production role\r\n         . ds-bob passes tsg-summariser-exec: DENIED (no identity policy allows it (implicit deny))\r\n  A13  blocked  Secret in the model definition: DescribeModel shows the Hugging Face token\r\n         . the model's Environment holds no secrets\r\n  A14  WORKED   Isolation dropped: an admin's quick test creates a model with no isolation and no VPC\r\n         . tsg-platform-admin CreateModel (EnableNetworkIsolation left out, no VpcConfig): allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n"]
[115.294846, "o", "         . tsg-platform-admin CreateModel (EnableNetworkIsolation false, no VpcConfig): allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n  A15  WORKED   Approval in a hurry: the approver approves a version that fails every check\r\n         . the ML lead approves version 3 in a hurry (pickle weights, no licence, no hashes): allowed (allowed by the identity policy)\r\n         . no approval gate: the status is now Approved and the pipeline deploys it\r\n\r\n  N1   works    The Helpdesk gets a ticket summary\r\n  N2   works    The pipeline deploys an approved version\r\n  N3   works    The ML lead approves a clean version\r\n  N4   works    A data scientist opens her own Studio profile\r\n  N5   works    A data scientist runs a job with the data science role\r\n  N6   works    The endpoint starts\r\n\r\nAttacks that worked: 2 of 15  (A14, A15)   |   normal requests that work: 6 of 6\r\n"]
